hadiths[9]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19273","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us from Zayd ibn Aslam from Ata ibn Yasar from Abu Abdullah al-Sunabihi who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sun rises between the two horns of Satan. When it rises it leaves it. When it is in the middle of the sky it joins it. When it declines or he said: Passes the zenith, it leaves it. When it nears setting it joins it. When it sets it leaves it. Do not pray these three hours."
"19274","Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mutarrif Abu Ghassan narrated to us, Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us from Ata ibn Yasar from Abu Abdullah al-Sunabihi that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever rinses his mouth and nostrils, his sins fall from his mouth and nose. Whoever washes his face, his sins exit from the edges of his eyes. Whoever washes his hands, they exit from his nails or from under his nails. Whoever wipes his head and ears, his sins exit from his head or the hair of his ears. Whoever washes his feet, his sins exit from his nails or under his nails. Then his steps to the mosque are supererogatory."
"19275","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mutarrif narrated to us from Zayd ibn Aslam from Ata ibn Yasar from Abu Abdullah al-Sunabihi from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever rinses and blows his nose, his sins exit from his nose and mouth, and he mentioned its meaning."
"19276","Attab ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Khalid ibn Said informed us from Qays ibn Abi Hazim from al-Sunabihi who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw an aged she-camel among the charity camels and was angry. He said: What is this? He said: O Messenger of Allah, I exchanged it for two camels from the outskirts of the charity. He fell silent."
"19277","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, al-Salt meaning Ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, he said: al-Harith ibn Wahb narrated to me from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sunabihi who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My ummah remains in a grasp while they do not act by three: while they do not delay Maghrib awaiting darkness imitating the Jews, while they do not delay Fajr until the stars fade imitating the Christians, and while they do not entrust funerals to their families."
"19278","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, and Ishaq narrated to us, Malik informed me from Zayd ibn Aslam from Ata ibn Yasar from Abdullah al-Sunabihi who said: When the servant performs wudu and rinses, sins exit from his nose. When he washes his face, sins exit from his face until they exit from under the edges of his eyes. When he washes his hands, his sins exit from his hands until they exit from under the nails of his hands. When he wipes his head, sins exit from his head until they exit from his ears. When he washes his feet, sins exit from his feet until they exit from under the nails of his feet. Then his walking to the mosque and his prayer are supererogatory for him."
"19279","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us from Ismail that he heard Qays say: I heard al-Sunabihi al-Ahmasi say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I am your forerunner at the Basin, and I will boast of you over the nations, so do not fight one another after me."
"19280","Rawh narrated to us, Malik and Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, they said: Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us from Ata ibn Yasar who said: I heard Abdullah al-Sunabihi say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The sun rises between the two horns of Satan. When it rises it joins it. When it rises high it leaves it. It joins it when it is level. When it passes the zenith it leaves it. Pray apart from these three hours."
"19281","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us from Abu Abdullah with the hadith of the sun."
